[0m[0m
The C project implements a "hydra" — a tree-based command menu system where commands are organized hierarchically by key characters. I translated all 14 functions from C to idiomatic Rust:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mCommand::new[0m — already provided, creates a new command node[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcommand_run[0m — prints the command string to stdout, returns length[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mcommand_add_child[0m — sorted insertion into the children linked list by key[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mfind_command[0m / [38;5;10mfind_command_mut[0m (helper) — linear search through children by key[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mtree_add_command[0m — recursively walks/creates the tree path from a key string, then inserts or updates the leaf command[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mprint_command[0m — formats and prints the command tree to stderr with ANSI colors, column layout[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mgetch[0m — reads a single byte from stdin[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mread_file[0m — reads entire file to string[0m[0m
